From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <pkgdemonteam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:03:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: drop uprintf output to the console tty while muted

cn_mute (patch 0062) drops kernel printf output to the console, but
uprintf() and tprintf() write straight to a process's controlling tty
through tty_putchar(), so anything the kernel tells a process whose
controlling tty is /dev/console still lands on the quiet boot screen,
and on the graphical splash with E19.

Drop TOTTY output while the console is muted when the tty is in use as
the console (TF_OPENED_CONS).  The message-buffer and log copies are
unchanged.  Unmuted boots (-v, -s, serial) are byte-identical.

Part of nextbsd/nextbsd#542 (nextbsd-kernel#371).
---
 sys/kern/subr_prf.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/kern/subr_prf.c b/sys/kern/subr_prf.c
index bbf81b7a4ffe6be54e7d71619016ca05b118bf6c..d7c23741a24d9df54dd75c91515f4bdbd57042d8 100644
--- a/sys/kern/subr_prf.c
+++ b/sys/kern/subr_prf.c
@@ -505,7 +505,13 @@ putchar(int c, void *arg)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if ((flags & TOTTY) && tp != NULL && !KERNEL_PANICKED())
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: while the console is muted, uprintf()/tprintf() to the
+	 * console tty is dropped like console output, so it cannot draw
+	 * on a quiet or graphical boot screen.
+	 */
+	if ((flags & TOTTY) && tp != NULL && !KERNEL_PANICKED() &&
+	    !(cn_mute && (tp->t_flags & TF_OPENED_CONS) != 0))
 		tty_putchar(tp, c);
 
 	if ((flags & TOCONS) && cn_mute) {
